    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and all tests pass. Build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded the `ownerSegment` field, `<TIER>_<AREA>`, to the owner representation.\n\n**Changes (3 files):**\n\n1. **New `util/OwnerSegment.java`** \u2014 a small, cohesive unit holding the whole rule. TIER is `PREMIUM` when membership level \u2265 3 else `STANDARD`; AREA is `METRO` when the locality is in `{NSW, VIC, QLD}` else `REGIONAL`. Self-contained, one tiny method (CC 3), no surrounding class complexity to carry.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line delegating to `OwnerSegment.of(...)`, reusing the existing `Membership.level(...)` and `CustomerCode.region(...)` derivations already used for the `membershipLevel` and `locality` fields. No method body changed.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the new read-only `ownerSegment` string property so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nI kept structural impact low by putting all the branching logic in a brand-new class with near-zero `WMC_other`, rather than growing any existing method or the large mapper. Tests: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `STANDARD_METRO` for a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW) and `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city.",
